#X text 240 83 Duffing Attractor;
#X text 240 108 Written by Paul Bourke;
#X text 240 133 ---;
#X text 240 158 The solution to the Duffing equations is often used
as an example of a classic chaotic system.;
#X text 240 198 The Duffing system of differential equations is:;
#X text 240 223 ===========;
#X text 240 248 dx / dt = y;
#X text 240 273 dy / dt = x - x3 - a y + b cos(w t);
#X text 240 298 ===================================;
#X text 240 323 where typically \, a = 0.25 \, b = 0.3 \, w = 1;
#X text 240 348 The following shows a "typical" segment of (x \, y)
values.;
